nd prepares potential counterplay with ...e5 or ...Qh4 in the future. It also avoids passive play.\n\nReason:  \nf7-f5 is a timely pawn lever that challenges White’s space advantage and accelerates Black’s development by opening the f-file for the rook. It creates immediate activity and avoids passive positioning.\n\nAnswer: P: f7-f5"}
